course: dictionary
lesson: 5673
title: Lizards and their clues
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A lizard is a kind of animal called a reptile. Its skin is scaly, it has four short legs, and it has a long tail. Sometimes the words around a new word tell you what it is. «A chameleon is a four-legged lizard» tells you that a chameleon belongs to the lizard group.
explain: Look at what the words around it do. «The Australian frilled lizard opens a huge neck frill and hisses to startle predators, and if that fails it runs off on its back legs.» A predator is an animal that hunts other animals, so the lizard is trying to scare away a danger.
explain: Groups help too. «Frogs, toads, newts and salamanders are amphibians; snakes, lizards, crocodiles and turtles are reptiles.» Lizards are listed with snakes and turtles, so you know a lizard is a reptile, not an amphibian.
fact: A lizard is a reptile with scaly skin, four short legs and a long tail.
fact: Geckos and iguanas are both kinds of lizard.
fact: Lizards are cold-blooded, so they bask in the sun to warm up.
fact: Some lizards can drop their tail to escape a predator, and then grow a new one.
fact: Do not grab wild lizards, and wash your hands after touching a pet lizard.
exercise: «A chameleon is a four-legged lizard.» What kind of animal is a lizard? | *A reptile with scaly skin | A bird with feathers | A fish that breathes with gills | A frog with smooth, wet skin
exercise: «Frogs, toads, newts and salamanders are amphibians; snakes, lizards, crocodiles and turtles are reptiles.» Which group is lizards in? | *Reptiles | Amphibians | Insects | Mammals
exercise: Lizards are cold-blooded, so they bask in the sun. What does bask mean? | *Lie in the sun to warm up | Shed their skin in the spring | Swim quickly through water | Hide in the dark to stay cool
test: Which lizard can climb walls? | *Gecko | Tortoise | Sparrow | Frog
test: Which lizard is named as the biggest lizard in this lesson? | *Komodo dragon | Gecko | Frilled lizard | Blue-tongue
exam: Which animal in this list is a lizard, not an amphibian? | Toad | Newt | Salamander | *Frilled lizard
